SUMMARY: Salsa Dura with Montreal Guests MARZOS & MATEO
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our last edition of BEDA · Put Trouble On My Tab!
 \n\nBEDA series is dedicated to the people who keep the city’s cultural a
 nd hospitality scene alive: musicians\, restaurant workers\, and tourism 
 professionals who rarely get to experience the events they help make poss
 ible. This five-month series offers a late performance on Sundays\, so th
 ose who work weekends can finally enjoy world-class live music. The proje
 ct also builds a cultural bridge between Toronto and Montreal\, inviting 
 exceptional artists from across provinces to share the stage and strength
 en connections within Canada’s music ecosystem\n\nMARZOS & MATEO\, winner
 s of the 18th edition of the Syli d'Or World Music Competition and recipi
 ents of the Afropop Worldwide Award 2025\, present a concert rooted in th
 eir Latin American origins and Afro-Caribbean heritage\, combining origin
 al compositions with salsa classics.\n\nMARZOS\, a modern salsa dura ense
 mble from Montreal\, brings together the power of a large-format orchestr
 a with a contemporary approach to Afro-Caribbean traditions. Known for it
 s precision\, musical direction and energetic performances\, the ensemble
  develops an original sound rooted in the diverse musical heritage of the
  Latin American diaspora.\n\nMATEO\, a Colombian singer-songwriter\, perf
 ormer and guitarist\, brings his own contemporary perspective to Latin mu
 sic\, blending Afrobeat\, alternative rock\, electro and Afro-Colombian s
 ounds.
CATEGORIES:Concert,Division-88
