BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877f0"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Short Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T193000
UID:69de5e272866a5b4884877f0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in joining a book club but are short on tim
 e?  Then join our Short Book Club\, where we read titles that are 250 page
 s or less. Meetings are held on the second Wednesday of each month.\nOur S
 eptember book is\nA Deadly Affair\nby Agatha Christie\nSummary: Love can 
 propel us to our greatest heights . . . and darkest depths. In this new co
 mpendium of Agatha Christie short stories\, witness the dark side of love-
 -crimes of passion\, games of the heart\, and deadly deceits. This pulse-p
 ounding compendium features beloved detectives Hercule Poirot and Miss Mar
 ple\, master of charades Parker Pyne\, the enigmatic Harley Quin\, and the
  adventurous Tommy and Tuppence\, all at the ready to solve tantalizing my
 steries.\nNew members are most welcome! Please inquire at the circulation 
 desk if you would like a copy of the book.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877f0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a58e693cca66c2f00a3c964"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC):  Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T200000
UID:6a58e693cca66c2f00a3c964@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC) workshops are unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect. (wcc-cec.org)\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. 
 Materials are provided.\nWorkshops are not sequential\;\nevery workshop is
  unique. Join ANY session and let’s write together!\nSpace is limited\n.
 \nRegistration required. Call us at 416-393-7683 for more information.
LOCATION:Wychwood\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a58e693cca66c2f00a3c964
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
