DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T150000
UID:6a7b419ac5fbcf8eb27ce816@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:***NEW RESCHEDULED DATE AND TIME***\nEmergencies can happen an
 ywhere at any time. In Canada\, we face numerous hazards\, including wildf
 ires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and earthquakes.\nThe\nBe\nReady workshop\na
 ims to raise individual and household emergency preparedness.\nIn this fre
 e workshop facilitated by the\nToronto Emergency Management Division of th
 e City of Toronto\n\, in partnership with the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, part
 icipants will learn about:\nThe potential hazards and risks in their area\
 nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow to assemble an emergency kit\nThe im
 portance of social and support networks during emergencies\nThis is a free
  drop-in program. No registration required.\nFor more information\, please
  contact the branch at\n416-394-1000.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - main floor
