BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Toronto Enterprise Devops User Group": "https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/events/315967192/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_toronto_enterprise_devops_user_group
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Enterprise DevOps
UID:event_315967192@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T042020Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T193000
SUMMARY:AI FinOps: The Next Frontier of DevOps Optimization
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Enterprise DevOps User Group\nWe spent years optimizin
 g cloud infrastructure\, right-sizing VMs\, tuning pipelines\, and fightin
 g surprise cloud bills. Now a new cost center has entered the chat: AI. Ev
 ery prompt\, every agent interaction\, every repository scan\, and every g
 enerated line of code consumes tokens—and those tokens add up quickly.\n
 \nAI coding assistants and agents like GitHub Copilot\, Claude Code\, and 
 OpenAI Codex are transforming how teams build software. But scaling AI ado
 ption without understanding consumption patterns is a bit like giving ever
 yone an unlimited cloud subscription and hoping for the best. (We all know
  how that story ends.)\n\nIn this session\, we'll explore AI FinOps practi
 ces for enterprise engineering teams: how to measure AI consumption\, opti
 mize token usage\, improve agent workflows\, manage context efficiently\, 
 choose the right models\, and get more value from every AI interaction.\n\
 nThrough practical examples with GitHub Copilot and modern AI coding agent
 s\, we'll apply familiar DevOps principles—visibility\, optimization\, g
 overnance\, and continuous improvement—to the next generation of softwar
 e delivery.\n\n*Come at 5:30 pm have some pizza and chat for a bit. The pr
 esentation starts at 6:00 pm.*
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/
 events/315967192/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260803T212347Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260803T212347Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
