DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T160000
UID:6a7b55f34cb69d003e2018d0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes.\nThe\nBe\nReady workshop\naims to raise individual and household
  emergency preparedness.\nIn this free workshop facilitated by the\nToront
 o Emergency Management Division of the City of Toronto\n\, in partnership 
 with the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, participants will learn about:\nThe poten
 tial hazards and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow
  to assemble an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and support networ
 ks during emergencies\nThis is a free drop-in program. No registration req
 uired.\nFor more information\, please contact the branch
