SUMMARY:Small Things: Making Inks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T180000
UID:evt-B4hdbvdZ2KFOB8O@events.lu.ma
DESCRIPTION:Address:\nScadding Court Community Centre\nGround Floor Kitche
 n\nToronto\, ON\nCanada\n\nSmall Things: Making Inks\nCome experiment with
  making inks crafted from found and natural materials. Play with different
  ink recipes and explore how the colours flow on the page. Follow your own
  curiosity\, and see where these handmade inks take you!\nThis workshop ta
 kes place on Sept 15\, and Sept 19.\nWorkshop facilitated by artist-educat
 or Heather Frise.\nHeather Frise is a filmmaker\, visual artist and educat
 or. Her work explores ecological imaginaries through drawing\, painting\, 
 film\, video\, animation\, and sound. She has been teaching drawing and ti
 me-based media at OCADU since 2015. Heather…\n\nHosted by Laboratory for
  Artistic Intelligence
LOCATION:Scadding Court Community Centre\, 707 Dundas St W\, Toronto\, ON 
 M5T 2W6\, Canada
URL:https://luma.com/dtw9fx72
X-SOURCE:Luma Toronto Discover
END:VEVENT
