SUMMARY:Good Morning\, Midnight by Lily Brooks-Dalton
DESCRIPTION:Post-Apocalyptic Book Club - Toronto Chapter\nThis time we'll 
 be reading *Good Morning\, Midnight* by Lily Brooks-Dalton. Here's the blu
 rb:\n\nAugustine\, a brilliant\, aging astronomer\, is consumed by the sta
 rs. For years he has lived in remote outposts\, studying the sky for evide
 nce of how the universe began. At his latest posting\, in a research cente
 r in the Arctic\, rumors of war arrive. The scientists are forced to evacu
 ate\, but Augustine stubbornly refuses to abandon his work. Shortly after 
 the others have gone\, Augustine discovers a mysterious child\, Iris\, and
  realizes the airwaves have gone silent. They are alone.\n\nAt the same ti
 me\, Mission Specialist Sullivan is aboard the Aether on its return flight
  from Jupiter. The astronauts are the first human beings to delve this dee
 p into space\, and Sully has made peace with the sacrifices required of he
 r: a daughter left behind\, a marriage ended. So far the journey has been 
 a success\, but when Mission Control falls inexplicably silent\, Sully and
  her crew mates are forced to wonder if they will ever get home.\n\nAs Aug
 ustine and Sully each face an uncertain future against forbidding yet beau
 tiful landscapes\, their stories gradually intertwine in a profound and un
 expected conclusion. In crystalline prose\, *Good Morning\, Midnight* pose
 s the most important questions: What endures at the end of the world? How 
 do we make sense of our lives?\n\nThe book is available here:\n\nAmazon- H
 ardcover\, Paperback\, eBook\, Audiobook:\nhttps://a.co/d/09erObPQ\n\nIndi
 go- Paperback:\nhttps://www.indigo.ca/products/good-morning-midnight?varia
 nt=46166439362737\n\nKobo- eBook:\nhttps://www.kobo.com/ca/en/ebook/good-m
 orning-midnight-1?sId=d4557681-b69a-4e68-931e-9c5bfbe6139d&ssId=Ot0g5Y1HiP
 hQuZozArWj8&cPos=1\n\nToronto Public Library:\nhttps://tpl.bibliocommons.c
 om/v2/record/S234C3411234\n\nLooking forward to seeing you there!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/post-apocalyptic-book-club-toronto-ch
 apter/events/315028316/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260530T191053Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260530T191053Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
