SUMMARY:Drag for Democracy!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T190000
UID:6a8860badb86e4004d86985e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:🪩🫰🪶 TORONTO!\nSashay away\nthe evening or\nmic\nat To
 ronto Public Library's Lillian H Smith Branch on September 17 at 5:30pm fo
 r stories\, poetry and readings exploring belonging\, community\, and what
  it means to show up for your city. Hosted by Carlotta Carlisle\, drop-in 
 and decide: is it SHADY not to vote? There is a municipal election in Toro
 nto on October 26\, and finding out why that matters can also be a fun eve
 ning out.\nOne thing is for sure\, this evening will bring together joy\, 
 laughter\, sharing and most certainly a little sass.\nIf you would like to
  read or share a short story\, poem or spoken word piece at our event\, ge
 t in touch with our team at\nhey@newmajority.ca\nThis event is organized b
 y New Majority\, a non-partisan non-profit supporting young people’s civ
 ic and democratic engagement across the country.\nRegistration recommended
 \, drop-ins are welcome.\nThere will be photography at the event\, please 
 let the organizers know if you do not wish to have your picture taken\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at 
 answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8860badb86e4004d86985e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
