BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b5b4be14820029886514"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Paul Theroux: True North\, On the Road in Canada
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T200000
UID:6a85b5b4be14820029886514@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For more than half a century\, Paul Theroux has traveled the g
 lobe and chronicled its far corners with curiosity\, wit\, and an unflinch
 ing eye. He joins us on stage to discuss his newest book\,\nTrue North\n\,
  in which he turns that eye to Canada.\nIn True North\, Theroux travels wi
 dely through remote villages\, multicultural cities\, and sweeping landsca
 pes that have defined modern Canada. Along the way\, he speaks with farmer
 s\, refugees\, writers like John Irving and Michael Ondaatje\, and Indigen
 ous leaders such as Tanya Talaga\, listening as Canadians reckon with iden
 tity\, belonging\, and patriotism\, often in response to the jabs and prov
 ocations of their southern neighbor.\nWith the empathy of a companion and 
 the sharpness of a cultural critic\, Theroux delivers a timely\, vivid tra
 vel narrative that reveals Canada as never before — diverse\, unsettled\
 , and alive with stories.\nIn conversation with acclaimed writer and criti
 c Charles Foran.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purc
 hase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nPaul Theroux\nCharles Foran\nRead mor
 e:\nTrue North : On the Road in Canada\nDeep South\nThe Tao of Travel\nMor
 decai\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toro
 nto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:
 00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket
  policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the greatest number of p
 eople have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or un
 til capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/w
 ine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is co
 mmitted to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would l
 ike to request accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleser
 vices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***
 \nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host loca
 l and international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about t
 heir new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey 
 following the program. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nThe Tao of Travel\nThe Tao o
 f Travel
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b5b4be14820029886514
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e344ca821f90037eda982"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:An Edible History of Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T200000
UID:6a7e344ca821f90037eda982@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto is a global culinary capital\, home to iconic food bra
 nds and restaurants\, from Café Diplomatico to Mr. Christie's Cookies. Bu
 t how did Toronto earn its reputation as a foodie haven? Join culinary his
 torian Dr. Laura Carlson on a mouth-watering journey through Toronto’s f
 ood history. Bring your appetite and your stretchy pants for a virtual tas
 te of past and present Toronto.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e344ca821f90037eda982
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
