SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd103@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Due to renovations the Bookclub will take place in Scadding Co
 urt Community Center in Room 4 (same building)\, participants will be resp
 onsible in sourcing copies of the monthly titles themselves as the branch
  will not be open to the public during this time. We apologize for the inc
 onvenience!\nBecome a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Cl
 ub! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a worl
 d of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming
 -of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something fo
 r everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thin
 gs up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fel
 low readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favo
 rite book? Join us and let's turn the page together!\nFriday September 18\
 n: The Covenant of Water by Abraham Verghese\nThe Covenant of Water\nby
  Abraham Verghese is a sweeping\, richly detailed novel set in Kerala\, In
 dia\, that follows a family across generations as they live with a mysteri
 ous condition in which some family members have a fear of water. Beginning
  in the early 1900s\, the story unfolds through the lives of several gener
 ations\, connecting their personal struggles\, relationships\, and secrets
  in unexpected ways. Blending family history\, love\, loss\, medicine\, fa
 ith\, and cultural traditions\, the novel explores how the past shapes gen
 erations to come. Verghese brings the landscape and people of Kerala vivid
 ly to life\, while weaving together themes of resilience\, sacrifice\, hea
 ling\, and the complicated bonds of family. It is an immersive and emotion
 al story that invites readers to become deeply invested in the lives of it
 s characters and the mysteries that connect them.
LOCATION:Sanderson - Closed\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd103
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
