SUMMARY: Frequency: NOONJEEM
DESCRIPTION:Sept 19\n\n8pm\n\n$15-$20 adv https://www.eventbrite.com/e/fr
 equency-noonjeem-tickets-1992238343515\n\n$25 doors\n\nJoin us for Freque
 ncy — a monthly live music series at Worth Gallery. Curated by our Sound 
 Director Janel Jones.\n\nFrequency spotlights BIPOC musicians of varying 
 genres through intimate\, stripped-back shows. Celebrating sound\, connec
 tion\, and creative expression in Toronto's vibrant music scene. Find you
 r new favorite musician in your new favorite gallery.\n\n\nThis month\, n
 oonjeem is grooving us into the night with mesmerizing music and vocals.\
 n\n\nAhmed Hegazy is a singer-songwriter\, music producer\, and performer
  who grew up in Cairo\, Egypt and is based in Toronto\, Ontario.\nUnder t
 he moniker of noonjeem\, he writes and produces his own music\, and perfo
 rms it across the city. His debut EP\, The Orchids Are Blooming! received
  praise from Toronto's The Grind. In it\, he splices soulful vocals with 
 experimental electronic production. Since its release\, he has performed 
 at events across the city including Long Winter\, Audiopollination\, and 
 FUFA\, and shared lineups with Vivek Shraya\, Janice Jo Lee and the QTs\,
  and Bahar Atish.
