CREATED:20260903T045325Z
DTSTART:20260920T180000Z
DTEND:20260920T200000Z
SUMMARY:Rally and March for Migrant Justice - by Migrant Rights Network
LOCATION:Christie Pits
DESCRIPTION:More info: https://actionnetwork.org/events/sep20to/\n\nHosted
  by Migrant Rights Network (https://migrantrights.ca)\n\nMigrants make
  Canada work. We care for children and elders\, grow food\, build homes\,
  and keep communities running. But the government is pushing migrants out
  instead of giving people equal rights. Join people across the country
  taking action to demand status for all\, permit renewals\, a stop to
  deportations\, and an end to exploitation!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:showuptoronto_static_showupto_ics
X-SOURCE:Show Up Toronto
UID:40339729-55eb-43c4-b18d-6e8d0fdd1a60
CREATED:20260903T050009Z
DTSTART:20260920T180000Z
DTEND:20260920T210000Z
SUMMARY:Understanding Capitalism: An Introduction to Capital - by The Leo
  Panitch School for Socialist Education
LOCATION:Virtual
DESCRIPTION:More info:
  https://www.tickettailor.com/events/panitchschool/2323358\n\nHosted by
  The Leo Panitch School for Socialist Education
  (https://leopanitchschool.ca/)\n\nWaking up from the capitalist nightmare
  requires a clear understanding of what we are up against: how we
  understand capitalism\, how it works\, and how it compels us to act in
  certain ways. This is the first of 7 week course to work through An
  Introduction to the Three Volumes of Karl Marx’s Capital by Michael
  Heinrich together.
END:VEVENT
