SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T153000
UID:69bee67b67801235ed73a990@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Don Mills Library and its neighbourhood is home to a varie
 ty of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry team to explore the n
 atural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize differe
 nt species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n
 Free program. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.
 \nRegistration is required.  Please register online.  Registration will 
 open on Monday\, August 10\, 2026.\nPresented as part of TPL’s environme
 ntal program series\, Our Fragile Planet. The series is generously support
 ed by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nThe tour will st
 art and end at the\nDon Mills Branch front lobby\nand will be guided by th
 e City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surf
 aces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoo
 r program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable sh
 oes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe incle
 ment weather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nIf yo
 u identify as a person with a disability and require an accessibility acco
 mmodation to participate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Se
 rvices by email\, accessibleservices@tpl.ca\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\
 , to make a request. Please contact us at least three weeks in advance.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Meeting location: front lobby.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bee67b67801235ed73a990
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults, Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8735dabe1482002988c539"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Digital Privacy 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T153000
UID:6a8735dabe1482002988c539@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested to learn how to maintain your online privac
 y and how to secure your online accounts and devices? If so\, this is the 
 class for you. Come and join us in this introductory session that is fille
 d with hands-on activities and discussion.\nIn this program\, you will:\nL
 earn how to maintain your online privacy through good habits and the secur
 ity of your accounts and devices.\nDevelop a strong password\, and review 
 the best methods for storing your passwords.\nLearn about various online t
 hreats: malware\, phishing\, hacking\, etc.\nGain an understanding of the 
 limitations of these tools and habits.
LOCATION:Northern District\, eLearning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8735dabe1482002988c539
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b4baf86ec588db26fd6ee"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:FULL - Seniors Digital Literacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T160000
UID:6a7b4baf86ec588db26fd6ee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is\nFULL.\nRichview Library will run Seniors Digi
 tal Literacy again January\n2027\n.  If you are interested in attending th
 e January session\,\nplease visit Richview Library to fill out an applicat
 ion.\nSeniors Digital Literacy\nis a\n6-week course\ndesigned to build you
 r confidence by introducing new skills slowly. At the end of the course\, 
 you may not know everything about the internet\, but you will have a\nsoli
 d foundation\nof\nnew skills\nand the\nconfidence\nto continue learning.\n
 Is This Course Right for You?\nFor seniors: beginners\, with\nvery\nlimite
 d or\nno\ncomputer experience\n*6 weeks:\nwith 1 class and 1 practice sess
 ion weekly (practice sessions take place on Thursdays from 2:00-3:30pm for
  the duration of the course)\n*Excluding the week of October 12th due to t
 he holiday closure.\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such as the mouse a
 nd the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, services and enter
 tainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and friends\nThe c
 lass is limited to 10 participants.  Please visit Richview Library to fi
 ll out an application form.
LOCATION:Richview\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7b4baf86ec588db26fd6ee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dc7ad4cb69d003e233fb0"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T153000
UID:6a8dc7ad4cb69d003e233fb0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse\nA class on how to us
 e a mouse for absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nI
 n this first session you will:\nObserve and practice how to operate a mous
 e effectively\nUnderstand various mouse pointers and cursors\nReview basic
  keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for basic Windows functions\nUpon compl
 etion of this class students will be able to use a computer mouse at a bas
 ic level and will be able to go online for additional practice.\nPrerequis
 ites: No computer experience required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstratio
 ns\nComputers for Beginners 2: Use the Keyboard\nA class on basic keyboard
  functions for absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\n
 In this second session you will:\nFamiliarize yourself through practice wi
 th the most essential keyboard functions (alphabet\, number and symbol key
 s)\nPractice proper keyboarding posture\nUpon completion of this class stu
 dents will be able to use a keyboard at a beginner level and know how to g
 o online for additional practice.\nPrerequisites: Computer for Beginners 1
  or basic mouse skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nComputers fo
 r Beginners 3: Use Windows\nA class on essential basic Windows skills for 
 absolute beginners with little computer experience.\nIn this third session
  you will:\nBecome familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPracti
 ce using common Windows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Wind
 ows\, Applications\nUpon completion of this class students will have a bas
 ic understanding of how to create and organize files in the Windows enviro
 nment.\nPrerequisites: Computer for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse and key
 boarding skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nComputers for Begin
 ners 4: Use the Internet\nAn introductory class on the Internet for absolu
 te beginners with little computer experience.\nIn this fourth session you 
 will:\nUnderstand how to read a web site address\nPractice using web addre
 sses\nSearch for information using a search engine\nExplore a web site in 
 detail to understand its key components\nUpon completion of this class stu
 dents will be able to use the internet at a beginner level and complete si
 mple searches.\nPrerequisites: Computer for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse
  and keyboarding skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nComputers f
 or Beginners 5: Use Google Search and Maps\nA class on using Google's filt
 ers\, tools\, and Maps for absolute beginners with little computer experie
 nce.\nIn this fifth session you will:\nUse Google search tools more effect
 ively to find websites\, images\, and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to f
 ind addresses and get directions for transit and road travel.\nUpon comple
 tion of this class students will be able to use more advanced search engin
 e features and use Google Maps at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: Computers
  for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills\nFor
 mat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nComputers for Beginners 6: Use Gmail\nL
 earn to use Gmail\, Google’s free web-based email service.\nIn this sixt
 h session you will:\nPractice basic email functions: send\, read\, reply\,
  forward\, delete email\, and attach files\nReview how spam and junk mail 
 work\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic understandi
 ng of how to use email.\nInstructions on how to set up and manage your own
  free Gmail account are included in the handout.\nPrerequisites: Basic key
 boarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
 4W 2G8.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Enhanced Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dc7ad4cb69d003e233fb0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8309aed4b10d003006fe4a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 2: Do More with your Data
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T150000
UID:6a8309aed4b10d003006fe4a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for beginners with li
 ttle or no Excel experience. Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills an
 d learn to use Excel data effectively.\nIn this second session\, you will:
 \nPractice data entry and formatting\nManipulate rows and columns\nCreate 
 and copy simple formulas\nConvert data to a Table then sort and filter\nCr
 eate your first chart\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to
  get more from your data using tables\, filters and charts.\nPrerequisites
 : Excel Basics Part 1 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard sk
 ills required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8309aed4b10d003006fe4a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
