SUMMARY:Adobe Photoshop II
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T153000
UID:6a87646f58433600542abc3c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this follow up to Photoshop I\, participants will explore a
 dditional tools in the Adobe Photoshop Toolbox that will help clean and e
 nhance photos faster and more accurately.\nWe'll also introduce you to a v
 ariety of new tools that include Filters\, Patches and of course Red Eye.
 \nAfter our first lesson finished by introducing you to layers\, we'll le
 vel up and create a layer mask while merging two photos together to get a 
 nice photo collage that can resemble a movie/book poster.\nRegistration is
  required. Registration opens up a week prior to the class at 9 a.m.\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
  and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how t
 he library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at
 \nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2
 G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a87646f58433600542abc3c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
