SUMMARY:Diaries of Mark Robinson Algonquin Park Ranger 1908-1936
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T150000
UID:6a7dc66e4c610f003894a90f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Gregory Klages presents Algonquin Diaries\, comprising the
  diary entries of Mark Robinson about life in Algonquin Park in the early 
 20th century. For over three decades\, Robinson served as ranger\, acting 
 Park Superintendent\, and officer in the Canadian Expeditionary Force. Thr
 oughout\, he maintained daily diaries in which he recorded his experiences
  of significant social\, political\, cultural and environmental events.\nD
 r. Klages is the author of\nThe Many Deaths of Tom Thompson: Separating Fa
 ct from Fiction\n\, a Writers' Trust of Canada Best Books 2016.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7dc66e4c610f003894a90f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5c9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Python Essentials 1 and 2 Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T153000
UID:6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5c9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Python and build your programming skills in a supportive
  group. This learning circle will meet on Tuesday afternoons from Septemb
 er 22 to December 8\, 2-3:30pm. Learning circles are study groups guided b
 y staff for people who want to take a free online course together in a wel
 coming space. Learners meet weekly and work together through the course ma
 terials. Participants are expected to commit to the duration of the course
  and attend all learning circle sessions.\nLearners who successfully compl
 ete both courses will earn a digital badge and certificate of completion.\
 nPython Essentials 1\nis the first in a 2-course series that teaches compu
 ter programming skills including how to design\, develop\, and improve com
 puter programs using the Python programming language. The course covers es
 sential programming topics such as data types\, variables\, control flow\,
  functions\, and exceptions.\nPython Essentials 2\nis the second in a 2-co
 urse series that will prepare you for the PCAP – Certified Associate in 
 Python Programming certification exam at Pearson VUE. This intermediate-le
 vel course covers advanced aspects of Python programming\, including modul
 es\, packages\, exceptions\, file processing and object-oriented programmi
 ng (OOP).\nFor more information about the Python learning circle\, please 
 contact\nnetworkingacademy@tpl.ca\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:York Woods
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5c9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61dda"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T153000
UID:6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61dda@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet weekly\,\nin-person\,\nevery Tuesday afternoon\, Se
 ptember 15 - December 8\, 2-3:30 PM (12 sessions).\nParticipants are expec
 ted to commit to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekl
 y basis.\nLearners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digita
 l badge\ndownload a certificate of completion
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61dda
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a878f6d60ccaf01c01fd03d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de la Bibliothèque de référence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T150000
UID:6a878f6d60ccaf01c01fd03d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aimez-vous lire en français ?  Avez-vous envie de participer 
 à des discussions autour des livres dans une ambiance détendue en toute 
 convivialité ?  Venez rejoindre le club de lecture pour échanger vos imp
 ressions\, pour analyser\, avec le regard d'autres lecteurs\, ce qui vous 
 a marqué\, et pour faire de belles découvertes littéraires.\nAu mois de
  septembre nous allons discuter\nRose à l'île\nde Michel Rabagliati.\nR
 ose à l'île\nVeuillez noter que ce programme s’adresse aux personnes f
 rancophones ainsi qu’à celles ayant un niveau avancé en français. Il 
 est nécessaire de pouvoir lire\, discuter et critiquer un livre avec une 
 aisance de communication en français.\nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre 
 français mais que vous avez plutôt un niveau débutant ou intermédiaire
 \, nous vous encourageons à découvrir nos\ncercles de conversation\nqui 
 ont lieu à la Bibliothèque de référence et aux succursales City Hall\,
  Cedarbare\, Northern District et Junction Triangle.\nACCESSIBILITÉ\nLe 
 sous-titrage en direct ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des 
 signes\, les services d’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement
  sont disponibles sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins d
 eux semaines à l’avance à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founders' Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a878f6d60ccaf01c01fd03d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
