SUMMARY:Your Vote Starts Here: Preparing for the 2026 Toronto Municipal El
 ection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T190000
UID:6a8c96c9392e9c02993c6344@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Toronto Municipal Election takes place on Monday\, Oc
 tober 26. Join Toronto Elections for an informative session covering every
 thing you need to know to cast your ballot with confidence. Learn about mu
 nicipal elections\, voting dates and times\, voting options\, and accessib
 ility supports available to voters.\nWe will also demonstrate\nMyVote\n\, 
 Toronto Elections' online tool that provides personalized voting informati
 on. Whether you're a first-time or future voter\, new to Toronto\, or simp
 ly looking to learn more about the municipal election process\, this sessi
 on will help you feel more informed and ready to participate in your local
  democracy.\nCheck out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate De
 mocracy\npage to learn more about Toronto’s upcoming municipal election\
 , access important voter resources\, and discover activities and interacti
 ve library programs for all ages happening at a branch near you.\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c96c9392e9c02993c6344
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
