UID:6a99a3cfe1fb8f13578bc17c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Orange Shirt Day and National Day for Truth and Reconciliation
  are observed annually on September 30. In this workshop\, Brianna Patrick
 \, Ojibway beading artist\, will explain the significance of Orange Shirt 
 Day and guide participants in the creation of individual Orange Shirt Day 
 pins that raise awareness and recognize the historical and ongoing trauma 
 that Indigenous peoples experience as a result of the residential school s
 ystem.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcom
 ing place for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff a
 re always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by
  a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
