SUMMARY:Gerrard/Ashdale Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T200000
UID:6a7e420eaafa6100295c7b50@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Gerrard/Ashdale book club meets once a month to discuss a 
 variety of books including fiction\, nonfiction\, and graphic novels.\nThi
 s month we will be reading\nFeeding Ghosts\na Pullizer nonfiction prize-wi
 nning graphic memoir by Tessa Hulls. In\nFeeding Ghosts\,\nHulls traces he
 r family’s migration from China to the US\, focusing on her grandmother\
 , a journalist in China during the communist takeover. The title refers to
  the ghosts that followed along the way during the immigration process.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e420eaafa6100295c7b50
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbc6fef89ee15800510929"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Elmbrook Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T200000
UID:69fbc6fef89ee15800510929@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us the last Thursday of each month to discuss that month'
 s title.  Haven't read the book?  Join us anyway to hear what others have 
 to say and meet new people. This is a drop in program.\nJuly 30 -\nMigrant
  Rain Falls in Reverse\nby\nVinh Nguyen\nAugust 27 -\nWhere’d You Go\, B
 ernadette?\nby Maria Semple\nSeptember 24 -\nMinistry of Time\nby\nKaliane
  Bradley\nOctober 29 -\nGreat Believers\nby\nRebecca Makkai\nNovember 26 -
 \nBlack Wolf\nby\nLouise Penny
LOCATION:Elmbrook Park\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbc6fef89ee15800510929
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6e4a8fb44674e2601c11c0"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Alderwood Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T200000
UID:6a6e4a8fb44674e2601c11c0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In\nErasing Memory\nby Scott Thornley\, Detective Superintende
 nt MacNeice investigates the haunting murder of a young violinist\, uncove
 ring connections to Eastern European history\, memory\, and loss while rel
 ying on his keen observational skills to solve an intricate crime.\n"Beaut
 ifully written." "A gripping tale."\nCopies of the book are available at A
 lderwood Branch in regular print. Ebook versions available from tpl.ca
LOCATION:Alderwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6e4a8fb44674e2601c11c0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
