BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7a064c4523092f0036262a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Shedding light on the dark side of the Universe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T200000
UID:6a7a064c4523092f0036262a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The standard model of cosmology tells us that the Universe is 
 mostly made up of ‘Dark Matter’\, with normal matter contributing only
  about 15% of the total budget. However\, direct detections have not yield
 ed any results about the nature of this mysterious dark matter\, leaving u
 s with only indirect means of inferring its existence and distribution. I 
 will try to answer tantalizing questions about its nature\, and how it may
  have helped shape the Universe.\nPresenter: Pratika Dayal\nSpecial thanks
  to the Dunlap Institute for Astronomy & Astrophysics at the University of
  Toronto.
LOCATION:St. Lawrence
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7a064c4523092f0036262a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
