DTSTAMP:20260905T042017Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T210000
SUMMARY:Fast Friends: Meet New People + Stay for 50+ Board Games | 25–45
DESCRIPTION:Toronto 20's to 50's Singles Social (4000+)\nYour next great c
 onversation could start over a drink\, a game\, or a simple “Hi.”\n\nJ
 oin us at Stout Irish Pub in Cabbagetown for a relaxed evening built aroun
 d actually getting to know people — not just standing around in a crowde
 d bar hoping someone starts a conversation.\n\nFast Friends gives you a li
 ttle structure to make meeting people easier: our host guides you through 
 short conversations and rotations\, then we open things up for games\, dri
 nks and further socialising.\n\n🎲 And yes — Stout has 50+ board games
 .\nSo once you've met the group\, you can grab a game with the people you 
 clicked with\, or simply stay for another drink and keep talking.\n\n🎟
 ️ Book Online & Save: [https://toronto26thsept.eventbrite.co.uk](https:/
 /toronto26thsept.eventbrite.co.uk)\nEarly Bird: CAD $10\nRegular: CAD $15\
 nAt the Door: CAD $20 cash — to host Kruttika\nBooking ahead helps us pl
 an the right group size and venue space — and your ticket confirms your 
 place.\n\n🤝 How the Evening Works\n7:00 PM — Arrive & Settle In\nMeet
  your host Kruttika\, grab a drink and get comfortable. If you're coming a
 lone\, that's completely normal — we'll help you get introduced.\n7:30 P
 M — Fast Friends\nThis is where the evening really gets going.\nYou'll m
 ove through a series of short\, guided conversations\, meeting different p
 eople along the way. You don't need to figure out who to approach or how t
 o start — we've designed the format to take care of that.\n✨ Common Gr
 ound Challenge\nWe'll introduce a simple interactive round to help you dis
 cover the unexpected things you have in common with people you've met.\nTh
 ink less “networking exercise” and more:\n“Wait… you like that too
 ?”\n\n🎲 From 8:30 PM — Board Games & Socialising\nStay and make an 
 evening of it.\nChoose from Stout's 50+ board games\, grab another drink\,
  find a few people to play with\, or simply continue the conversations tha
 t started during Fast Friends.\n\nAnd if you're staying later\, Stout's cu
 rrent After Dark Special runs from 9–11 PM\, with $7 beers and $7 highba
 lls\, among other specials.\n\n❤️ Why This Isn't Just Another Social\n
 ✔️ Meet 15–25 new people in one evening\n✔️ A professionally hos
 ted format — you don't have to work the room yourself\n✔️ Guided con
 versations and rotations\n✔️ Common Ground Challenge\n✔️ 50+ board
  games available afterwards\n✔️ Relaxed Irish-pub atmosphere\n✔️ M
 ost people attend solo\n✔️ Time to stay and socialise after the hosted
  rounds\n✔️ Friendship-focused\, not a dating event\n\n👋 Who Should
  Come?\nWhether you've just moved to Toronto\, have lived here for years\,
  or simply feel like your social circle could use some new faces\, you're 
 welcome.\nAges 25–45\nSolo attendees welcome\nNew faces always welcome\n
 This is about friendship\, conversation and building your social circle 
 — not dating.\n📍 Stout Irish Pub\n221 Carlton St\, Toronto\n\n🌍 Fa
 st Friends\nFor over 10 years\, Fast Friends has been bringing people toge
 ther through professionally hosted social events in 30+ cities worldwide.\
 nCome for the conversations. Stay for the games. Leave with new connection
 s. ❤️
