SUMMARY:Book Club: Harlem Shuffle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T160000
UID:6a88b79769166f088b93e052@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In 1960s Harlem\, Ray Carney owns his own furniture store and 
 is determined to prove himself as an honest businessman\, in stark contras
 t to his crooked dead father. But Carney has never been completely clean\,
  and he supplements his income by fencing stolen goods.\nJoin us for a cha
 t about the book Harlem Shuffle by Colson Whitehead\nThis is a registered 
 program\, you can register online and pick up a copy of the book in branch
 .
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a88b79769166f088b93e052
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
