LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T193212Z
UID:10002019-1790879400-1790884800@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Introduction to Bonsai 101
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging talk on the art of Bonsai!\nThis introductory Bonsai course focuses on the origins of the Bonsai practice\, the practical “craft” side of the artform\, the cultural influences and the basics of production\, development\, and care of Bonsai.\n \nThursday\, October 1\, 6:30 to 8 p.m.\nPublic $20\, TBG Members $15 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Josh Chang\nJosh Chang is the current sitting President of the Toronto Bonsai Society. His practice encompasses his personal collection of over 200 trees in various stages of development. Josh has been practicing the hobby for nine years now\, and has taught the practice to many people over the last seven years. Josh believes that everyone has the capacity to learn the artform and practice the hobby.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/introduction-to-bonsai-101/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dff97b849fe0ad509bbb80b242e61d85.jpg
END:VEVENT
