SUMMARY:Shea Butter: Natural Skin Care & Everyday Wellness - Wellness Work
 shop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T110000
UID:6a8f50a7660e510bf4401ea0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​This educational wellness workshop explores the benefits of
  shea butter and natural ingredients for skin hydration and everyday self-
 care. Participants will learn how traditional ingredients support healthy 
 skin and simple wellness routines. The program includes a short presentati
 on and demonstration of how natural body care formulas are created.\nParti
 cipants take home their personalized shea butter blend\nDisclosure: This p
 rogram uses non-consumable scented products that can be applied to the ski
 n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f50a7660e510bf4401ea0
