BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-all-levels-fall-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T203000
DTSTAMP:20260805T182842Z
CREATED:20260805T182842Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T182842Z
UID:146279-1791307800-1794342600@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Hand Building (All Levels)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building (All Levels)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Tuesdays October 6 to November 10\, 2026\n5:30 pm – 8:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \nMake functional\, sculptural\, and decorative pieces using hand-building techniques. Practice sculpting\, slab building\, coiling\, surface decoration\, and glazing. This 6-week class is open to potters at all levels. \n\nThis class includes access to a 10kg bag of clay\, glazes and underglazes. Additional bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $315\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $370\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: October 6\, 13\, 20\, 27\, November 3\, 10\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Pinch pots and coiling\nWeek 2: Slab building\nWeek 3: Introduction to glazing\nWeek 4: Attaching decorations and handles\nWeek 5: Studio time\nWeek 6: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie Fisher\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie is a passionate young artist with more than 15 years of experience teaching art to students of all ages. She is formally trained in drawing\, painting\, photography\, printmaking\, and sculpture. She recently received her Masters in Expressive Arts Therapy from the University of Hong Kong. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-all-levels-fall-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Adult-Class-Thumbnail-1.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
