DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T190000
UID:6a492906541102b7fa8a625a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aqua Nibii Waawaaskone​ provides Indigenous learning through
  an interactive performance and workshop of hand drums\, shakers and smudg
 e medicines. Each song teaches about the history and traditions of the Ind
 igenous Peoples of Turtle Island\, also known as North America.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a492906541102b7fa8a625a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
