SUMMARY:Vector Design with Adobe Illustrator
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T200000
UID:6a721b2c0d65ac3600444c98@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a 2-part series\, participants are expected to attend 
 both sessions.\nLearn how to make digital art in Adobe Illustrator. We wil
 l talk about the differences between vector and raster images\, explore so
 me of the tools at our disposal\, and then use these tools to design a sma
 ll vector drawing. In the second class we will learn more advanced techniq
 ues.\nThis class is for beginners but assumes you have a basic understandi
 ng  of computer skills.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto \nPublic Library under th
 e Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, \nand 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program \nregistration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library \nhandles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Ethennonnhawahstihnen'\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a721b2c0d65ac3600444c98
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
