X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T203000
DTSTAMP:20260805T182842Z
CREATED:20260805T182842Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T182842Z
UID:146325-1791394200-1795638600@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Sculptural Pottery: Stoneware (All Levels)
DESCRIPTION:Sculptural Pottery: Stoneware (All Levels)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Wednesdays October 7 to November 25\, 2026\n5:30 pm – 8:30 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \n\nUsing stoneware clay\, push your ideas beyond the functional into the sculptural. Learn to think outside the box\, using hand-building techniques to make and decorate small sculptural forms at your own pace. This 8-week class is suitable for all skill levels. \nThis class includes access to one 10kg bag of stoneware clay\, glazes and underglazes. Additional bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: October 7\, 14\, 21\, 28\, November 4\, 11\, 18\, 25 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nWeek 1: Introduction and pinch demo\nWeek 2: Advanced pinching and intro to coiling\nWeek 3: Building with coils\nWeek 4: Intro to slab building\nWeek 5: Combining techniques\nWeek 6: Studio time and underglaze demo\nWeek 7: Studio time\nWeek 8: Glazing\n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Mohammad Tabesh\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Mohammad Tabesh is a Toronto-based multidisciplinary artist whose work delves into the complexities of the human experience\, resistance\, and social change. Across various mediums\, including writing\, printmaking\, multimedia\, and sculpture\, Mohammad strives to convey deeply human and universal stories. His work has been recognized with several Canada Council for the Arts grants and an Access Copyright Foundation grant. Mohammad earned his BFA from OCAD University and was honoured as the recipient of the Sculpture and Installation Medal in 2020. In 2022\, he was accepted as an Artist-in-Residence for ceramics at Harbourfront Centre. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/sculptural-pottery-stoneware-all-levels-fall-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Adult-Class-Thumbnail-4.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/wheel-throwing-stoneware-intermediate-fall-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T203000
DTSTAMP:20260805T182842Z
CREATED:20260805T182842Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T182842Z
UID:146327-1791394200-1795638600@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Wheel Throwing: Stoneware (Intermediate)
DESCRIPTION:Wheel Throwing: Stoneware (Intermediate)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Wednesdays October 7 to November 25\, 2026\n5:30 pm – 8:30 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nAdvance your skills working with stoneware on the pottery wheel to create functional and sculptural vessels. This 8-week class is designed for students who have some experience using the pottery wheel. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of stoneware clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    SOLD OUT\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: October 7\, 14\, 21\, 28\, November 4\, 11\, 18\, 25 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Throwing and analyzing cylinders\nWeek 2: Throwing on bat and throwing large pieces\nWeek 3: Trimming and refining\nWeek 4: Glazing\nWeek 5: Closed form and lidded pots\nWeek 6: Knobs and handles\nWeek 7: Trimming and refining works\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Annika Hoefs\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Annika Hoefs is a Toronto-based artist and educator\, specializing in ceramics. She holds a Bachelor of Material Art and Design from OCAD University where she initially focused on textiles\, but graduated with a full concentration in ceramics. Alongside her studio practice\, she has been teaching ceramic classes to students of all ages and skill levels since 2016. Annika’s functional and sculptural ceramics can be found in select gallery shops\, restaurants\, and luxury hotels\, locally and internationally. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/wheel-throwing-stoneware-intermediate-fall-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Wheel-Class-Thumbnail.jpg
