SUMMARY:An Introduction to Data Visualization and Storytelling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T193000
UID:6a96f2bd5e6fc10d0550c5d0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Participate in an in-person program to learn data visualizati
 on\, storytelling\, and data literacy\, equipping participants with essent
 ial skills to transform data into compelling visual narratives. You will l
 earn about the most popular data visualization types\, best practices in d
 ata preparation\, and techniques for selecting effective charts. Through h
 ands-on exercises\, you will practice creating clear\, impactful visualiza
 tions that communicate data insights effectively. This course is ideal for
  those who want to enhance their data storytelling skills and build a stro
 ng foundation in data visualization.\nPrerequisites: Excel Basics Part 1 o
 r equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.
LOCATION:McGregor Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96f2bd5e6fc10d0550c5d0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4dfc3b6c71003e5de6c9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Peek Inside an AI Assistant: How It Thinks and Works
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T200000
UID:6a9b4dfc3b6c71003e5de6c9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've asked an AI chatbot questions. But there's another kind
  of AI that doesn't just answer: it acts.\nIn this demo-driven talk\, we'l
 l look deeply at always-on personal AI assistants. The assistant can read 
 your files\, use your apps\, and remember what you've told it\, growing mo
 re useful over time. The same powers that let it help you can hurt you if 
 something goes wrong. We'll also open up what happens inside: the hidden i
 nstructions\, the tools it uses\, what it remembers and forgets.\nThen we'
 ll look at the AI assistant that helped develop this workshop\, and how we
  shaped our workflow together\, and why.\nRegistration is required and wil
 l start September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaran
 teed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nInformation Collection 
 Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto
  Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, 
 and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registr
 ation\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles y
 our information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\
 n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4dfc3b6c71003e5de6c9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90738c6383850d1b2453d3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Financial Literacy & Tax Management for Newcomer Entrepreneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T200000
UID:6a90738c6383850d1b2453d3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Navigating self-employment in a new country can be challeng
 ing\, but this workshop will equip newly immigrated entrepreneurs with the
  essential financial tools to succeed in Canada. This workshop is designe
 d to build your confidence in managing your business finances and help you
  thrive as a self-employed professional in Canada. Perfect for newcomers l
 ooking to establish a solid financial foundation.​\nThis program is part
  of Small Business Month and the Newcomer Entrepreneurship Initiative.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
 ions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for even
 t and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how 
 the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff a
 t\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Earlscourt room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90738c6383850d1b2453d3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
