SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Recycled Papermaking with Paper Powered Workshops
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T164500
UID:6a988faaaafa610029611ca7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to make environmentally-friendly\, recycled\, handma
 de paper in this fun\, easy\, and interactive workshop. Leave with sheets 
 of beautiful\, one-of-a-kind paper plus the knowledge that you did somethi
 ng great for the earth!\nParticipants will learn about the ancient craft o
 f papermaking\, and have an opportunity to make their own beautiful\, recy
 cled paper from paper scraps\, plus a variety of techniques to further cus
 tomize their sheets.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hub
 s are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where h
 elpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered d
 aily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out 
 more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a988faaaafa610029611ca7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
