SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Orange Shirt Day Beaded Pin Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T170000
UID:6a8dcffadb86e4004d871de9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Orange Shirt Day and National Day for Truth and Reconciliation
  are observed annually on September 30. In this workshop\, Brianna Patrick
 \, Ojibway beading artist\, will explain the significance of Orange Shirt 
 Day and guide participants in the creation of individual Orange Shirt Day 
 pins that raise awareness and recognize the historical and ongoing trauma 
 that Indigenous peoples experience as a result of the residential school s
 ystem.\nDrop in. No registration required.\nFriday\, October 9\, 2026 at 4
  – 5 PM\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a wel
 coming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staf
 f are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop
  by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dcffadb86e4004d871de9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
