SUMMARY:Introduction to OnShape (Teens)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T190000
UID:6a9464cb29a7dd0d6747c932@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in creating your own 3D models? Join us for an intr
 oduction to Onshape\, a powerful cloud-based Computer-Aided Design (CAD) s
 oftware used by engineers\, designers\, and makers around the world.\nIn t
 his beginner-friendly workshop\, participants will learn the fundamentals 
 of 3D modeling\, including how to navigate the Onshape interface\, create 
 basic sketches\, and turn those sketches into 3D objects using extrude and
  extrude cut features. No previous CAD experience is required.\nBy the end
  of the program\, participants will have created their own simple 3D model
  and gained the skills needed to continue exploring CAD design on their ow
 n.\nBasic Computer skills are Mandatory\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9464cb29a7dd0d6747c932
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e24aafa61002961b09b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Make Your Own Interactive Story with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T200000
UID:6a9b4e24aafa61002961b09b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could write a story where the reader chooses what 
 happens\, like a branching adventure\, a mystery\, or a game\, and have AI
  build it with you?\nIn this class\, you'll learn "vibe-coding": using an 
 AI coding assistant to build your own interactive story or simple game. Yo
 u'll design the branches\, describe the rules in plain language\, test for
  the tricky edge cases (what if the player picks the weird option?)\, and 
 end up with a single file you can share with anyone. Just a story you want
  to tell. This is the playful sibling of the practical vibe-coding worksho
 p.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be gua
 ranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nPrivacy and Risk Mes
 sage\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activ
 ities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do
  not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are e
 ncouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which 
 include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privac
 y statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nL
 earn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLear
 n more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more
  about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
