X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dd3dd57c264087ad3a807"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T153000
UID:6a8dd3dd57c264087ad3a807@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC)\nworkshop is unlike any oth
 er. We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\,
  listen deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into 
 your story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\,
  and respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials ar
 e provided. Workshops are not sequential\; every workshop is unique - join
  in at any session and let's write together!\nSpace is limited. Drop in\, 
 no registration required. Please arrive a few minutes early. For more inf
 ormation\, please contact the branch.\n​Presented by Writers Collective 
 of Canada (WCC)\, a charitable arts-health organization that ignites conne
 ction through creativity by inspiring powerful\, authentic stories shared 
 in community.\nhttps://wcc-cec.org/\nAccessibility\nLive or automated clos
 ed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, intervenor services\, or at
 tendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at
  least 2 weeks in advance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-events.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dd3dd57c264087ad3a807
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90a2db1c197d11325b4eb0"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 1: Create a Simple Spreadsheet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T153000
UID:6a90a2db1c197d11325b4eb0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for absolute beginner
 s with little or no Excel experience.\nIn this first session\, you will:\n
 Learn the basic function and design of Excel files\nPractice basic data en
 try for text\, numbers\, and basic functions: Sum\, AutoSum and Average\nC
 reate and save your first workbook and worksheets\nUpon completion of this
  class\, you will be able to use Excel at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: B
 asic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demons
 trations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90a2db1c197d11325b4eb0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
