SUMMARY:ABCD Reads "Salvation of a Saint" by Keigo Higashino
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads "**[Salvation of a S
 aint](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C2888913)**" by Keigo Hi
 gashino.\n\n[RESULTS of the poll for this event]\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::
 **\n"The Devotion of Suspect X was a hit with critics and readers alike. T
 he first major English language publication from the most popular bestsell
 ing writer in Japan\, it was acclaimed as "stunning\," "brilliant\," and "
 ingenious."\nNow physics professor Manabu Yukawa—Detective Galileo—ret
 urns in a new case of impossible murder\, where instincts clash with facts
  and theory with reality.\nYoshitaka\, who was about to leave his marriage
  and his wife\, is poisoned by arsenic-laced coffee and dies. His wife\, A
 yane\, is the logical suspect—except that she was hundreds of miles away
  when he was murdered. The lead detective\, Tokyo Police Detective Kusanag
 i\, is immediately smitten with her and refuses to believe that she could 
 have had anything to do with the crime. His assistant\, Kaoru Utsumi\, how
 ever\, is convinced Ayane is guilty. While Utsumi's instincts tell her one
  thing\, the facts of the case are another matter. So she does what her bo
 ss has done for years when stymied—she calls upon Professor Manabu Yukaw
 a.\nBut even the brilliant mind of Dr. Yukawa has trouble with this one\, 
 and he must somehow find a way to solve an impossible murder and capture a
  very real\, very deadly murderer.\nSalvation of a Saint is Keigo Higashin
 o at his mind-bending best\, pitting emotion against fact in a beautifully
  plotted crime novel filled with twists and reverses that will astonish an
 d surprise even the most attentive and jaded of readers." (from [Macmillan
  Publishers](https://us.macmillan.com/books/9781250036278/salvationofasain
 t/))\n\n"When a man is discovered dead by poisoning in his empty home his 
 beautiful wife\, Ayane\, immediately falls under suspicion. All clues poin
 t to Ayane being the logical suspect\, but how could she have committed th
 e crime when she was hundreds of miles away?\nAs Tokyo police detective Ku
 sanagi tries to unpick a seemingly unrelated sequence of events he finds h
 imself falling for Ayane. When his judgement becomes dangerously clouded h
 is assistant must call on an old friend for help\; it will take a genius t
 o unravel the most spectacular web of deceit they have ever faced…\nSALV
 ATION OF A SAINT is a magnificently complex and page-turning thriller star
 ring international crime fiction’s most enigmatic sleuth.This is essenti
 al reading for all fans of exceptional crime fiction." (from [Hachette UK]
 (https://www.hachette.co.uk/titles/keigo-higashino/salvation-of-a-saint/97
 80349138817/))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to arrive 30 
 minutes before the event and stay 30 minutes or longer afterward to connec
 t with other attendees outside the book talk.\n\nPlease ensure you have re
 ad the book before attending (though finishing any book is not a barrier t
 o participating\, as long as you don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst-time atten
 dees can join for free. If the event is full\, we maintain an unofficial w
 aitlist. Please send [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/members/55295192/) a
  direct message for more information\, in either case.\n\nWe request a $3 
 contribution from regular attendees to help cover our monthly meetup costs
 .\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each event\, we will ask
  for nominees for our next book. If you have a good one in mind\, please e
 nsure it is between 200-400 pages long\, available from the Toronto Public
  Library\, and counts as contemporary literary fiction (though these are n
 ot hard and fast rules). When enough nominees are collected\, Michael will
  send the members a direct message with a link where you can vote.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/a-book-club-downtown-abcd/events/3160
 11630/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T231232Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260806T231232Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
