SUMMARY:PowerPoint Basics 3: : Add Visual Style to your Presentation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T153000
UID:6a906d6f4cb69d003e23c5e1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Create a more sophisticated Microsoft PowerPoint presentation 
 with more advanced features.\nIn this third session\, you will learn to:\n
 - Crop pictures\, add picture borders and add picture effects\n- Align and
  distribute objects\n- Insert and edit SmartArt graphics\n- Animate object
 s\n- Edit a theme\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to enh
 ance your PowerPoint presentations with audiovisual elements.\nPrerequisit
 es:  PowerPoint Basics Part 1 and 2 or equivalent experience. Keyboarding 
 and mouse skills required.\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a906d6f4cb69d003e23c5e1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
