BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f240ebe148200298a3f02"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Halloween Movie Night: Five Nights at Freddy's
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T170000
UID:6a8f240ebe148200298a3f02@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Halloween with a scary movie in the Youth Hub. Join 
 us for a screening of Five Nights at Freddy's (110 min).\nDrop in\, all te
 ens welcome.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a 
 welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful s
 taff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. D
 rop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f240ebe148200298a3f02
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6978ce85491b809c6f1577d8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Itty Bitty Knitty Committee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T190000
UID:6978ce85491b809c6f1577d8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join knitters and other fibre artists of all levels for a cozy
  hour in a knitting circle! Exchange tips and tricks\, bring your projects
 \, troubleshoot patterns\, or work on that piece you’ve been wanting to 
 try.\nPlease note: t\nhis is not a class.\nRegistration is optional if you
  would like reminders and any cancellation notices.\n*Please note that the
 re is currently no public parking available at the branch*\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, FCCR (program room on the main floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6978ce85491b809c6f1577d8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Preschool": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dbb0560ccaf01c020e17d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_preschool
SUMMARY:Halloween Howl
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T190000
UID:6a8dbb0560ccaf01c020e17d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate spooky season with Halloween songs\, rhymes and book
 s. These not-so-scary stories will have kids howling with laughter the nig
 ht before the big day! After the stories\, kids can complete their own hau
 nted house craft. Costumes are welcome!\nFor children ages 2-6 and their 
 caregivers. Drop in.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Children's Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8dbb0560ccaf01c020e17d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a932b6c3b6c71003e5c470b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Adult Horror Movie Screening: 1BR
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T193000
UID:6a932b6c3b6c71003e5c470b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for spooky season with a screening of 1BR (2020) by di
 rector David Marmor.\nAfter leaving behind a painful past to follow her dr
 eams\, Sarah scores the perfect Hollywood apartment. But something is not 
 right. Unable to sleep\, tormented by strange noises and threatening notes
 \, her new life quickly starts to unravel. By the time she learns the horr
 ifying truth\, it's too late. Caught in a waking nightmare\, Sarah must fi
 nd the strength to hold onto her crumbling sanity\, or be trapped forever 
 in an existential hell.\nRuntime: 90 minutes.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd Floor\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a932b6c3b6c71003e5c470b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
