BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51982dac6e0037243871"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:AI for Small Business and Entrepreneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T160000
UID:6a9b51982dac6e0037243871@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've got the business idea. Now come the thousand questions:
  who's my customer\, what's the market\, how do I pitch this?\nIn this cla
 ss\, you'll use AI as a research and planning partner for small business. 
 We'll practice together on a sample business\, turning rough ideas into bu
 siness plans\, digging into markets\, drafting customer-discovery question
 s\, and building useful low-maintenance automation. The most valuable thin
 g you'll get is usually a better question to be tested in the real world. 
 Whether you're starting or growing\, you'll leave with an experiment you c
 an run on your own business this week.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboardin
 g and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience requ
 ired.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 P
 M.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of
  the program.\nPrivacy and Risk Message\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This P
 rogram\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed
  below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account fo
 r this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s gu
 idance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe
  encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to atte
 nding this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privac
 y policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\
 nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGo
 ogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51982dac6e0037243871
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
