UID:6a9b51a1aafa61002961b297@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build your own personal library app\, just b
 y describing it?\nIn this class\, you'll use an AI coding assistant to bui
 ld a small app for your reading life: add books you've read and books you 
 want to read\, keep your whole list in one private place\, and link each b
 ook to the library catalogue so placing a hold is one click away. You'll l
 earn the build loop: describe what you want\, review the plan\, build one 
 feature\, test it\, fix the bugs. Your reading list stays on your own comp
 uter. The library keeps the books\; this file keeps your reading life\, an
 d it travels with you.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet s
 kills. Computers are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistrat
 ion is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your s
 pot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nP
 rivacy and Risk Message\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis pro
 gram includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on libra
 ry laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\
 nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughou
 t sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you t
 o review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this progr
 am:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude
  Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gra
 vity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\n
 Learn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a1aafa61002961b297
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
