BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Build Your First App with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop\, you'll 
 use an AI coding assistant to build your own small\, useful webpage\, chec
 klist\, or organizer from scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe w
 hat you want\, review the plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bug
 s\, and write documentation so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nP
 rerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are pro
 vided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will 
 start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guarantee
 d after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nPrivacy and Risk Message\n
 About the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activities 
 that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not n
 eed to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are encoura
 ged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which includ
 e best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy stat
 ements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn m
 ore about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more
  about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about
  the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
