BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a9aafa61002961b2a1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:AI for Job Hunting: Build Your Own System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6a9b51a9aafa61002961b2a1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Job hunting is a job in itself: applications\, deadlines\, int
 erviews\, follow-ups. What if you could build your own AI-powered system t
 o help you manage it?\nIn this hands-on class\, you'll explore a job-hunti
 ng dashboard built with AI: how it tracks applications\, sets automatic al
 erts for postings that match you\, and practices interviews with you throu
 gh role-play. You'll leave with the templates to build your own. We'll als
 o talk about how employers screen applications\, and how it can make thing
 s unfair. Come explore a tool that works for you\, not the other way aroun
 d.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nPrivacy and Risk Mess
 age\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activi
 ties that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do 
 not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are en
 couraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which i
 nclude best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy
  statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLe
 arn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more 
 about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more abo
 ut the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the
  tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a9aafa61002961b2a1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
