BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Access to Housing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T160000
UID:6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you seeking housing support or have questions about afford
 able housing options? Join us at S. Walter Stewart Library for personalize
 d\, one-on-one assistance with a Housing Services Worker.\nEast York Housi
 ng Help Hub is offering information session on the Rent Geared to Income o
 ptions available in\nMyAccesstoHousingTO\nonline system. Housing staff wil
 l support program participants with hands-on supports and help them comple
 te the registration process.\nFor more information or to register please c
 ontact East York Housing Help Hub at 416 698-9306 or email eyhhc@eyetfrp
 .ca.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f559c2866a5b4883e53bc"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Mystery Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T140000
UID:699f559c2866a5b4883e53bc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you like mystery books? Join a group of mystery lovers for 
 informal discussions. There is no set book each month\, come share your f
 avourite books and learn about new authors.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:City Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f559c2866a5b4883e53bc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a837ec969166f088b92e322"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: One False Move
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T150000
UID:6a837ec969166f088b92e322@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of One False Move movie.\nA small-town police chief conceals an explosive
  secret. A pair of ruthless drug dealers leave a bloody trail in their wak
 e as they make their way from Los Angeles to Arkansas. And an enigmatic wo
 man is caught in the middle. The way these desperate lives converge become
 s a masterclass in slow-burn tension thanks to the nuanced direction of Ca
 rl Franklin\, whose haunting debut feature travels a crooked road across A
 merica’s most fraught divisions—urban and rural\, Black and white—wh
 ile imbuing noir conventions with a wrenching emotional depth.\nRated R. 1
 hr 45mins.\nEnglish Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when 
 available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a837ec969166f088b92e322
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
