SUMMARY:Stretch and Strength for Seniors -Tuesdays: Fall2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T120000
UID:tribe-10102242@scaddingcourt.org
DESCRIPTION:FREESeniors’ stretch and strength program builds independenc
 e by improving balance\, mobility\, and daily function through controlled 
 exercises like seated stretches\, bodyweight movements. The program focuse
 s on increasing flexibility\, muscle mass\, and coordination to prevent fa
 lls\, reduce stiffness\, and enhance overall well-being\, often incorporat
 ing warm-ups\, strength sets with modifications (like chair support) and c
 ooldowns with deep breathing.Fall 2026 session:Tuesdays: 11 am – 12 pm T
 hursday
LOCATION:Scadding Court Community Centre\, 707 Dundas Street West\, Toront
 o
URL:https://scaddingcourt.org/event/stretch-and-strength-for-seniors-tuesd
 ays-fall2026/2026-12-01/
X-SOURCE:Scadding Court Community Centre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2763"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T130000
UID:6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2763@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Tuesdays\, join us for crafts
  (11am-1pm) a walk (11:15am-1pm) and chair yoga (11:30am-12:30pm).\nSnacks
  and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will
  be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGer
 stein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Varies by program
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2763
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69583000c719ac98c335c8db"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T163000
UID:69583000c719ac98c335c8db@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nTHHC can be contacted at 416-285-8070.
LOCATION:Malvern
