DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T180000
UID:6a87558c60ccaf01c01fbd32@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect matches older adults with a teen volunteer t
 o provide tech help\, under the guidance of library staff. Learn the basic
 s of using smart phones\, tablets\, and laptops\nand learn about topics su
 ch as\ninstant messaging\, social media\, and file management\n. Get one o
 n one support in a welcoming and friendly environment.\nWe DO NOT help wit
 h printers or printing. Please bring your device with you to the program.\
 nIf you're a teen between the ages of 13-17 and would like to learn more a
 bout becoming a Seniors E-Connect volunteer\, visit the\nSeniors E-Connect
  Volunteering page\nor contact the branch.\nInformation Collection Notice:
 \nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public
  Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(
 d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\,
  delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inf
 ormation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416
 -397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Yorkville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a87558c60ccaf01c01fbd32
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
